This is my first ascension, so I didn't worry about conducts.  My only
conduct is no bone piles because finding bone piles of my previous
characters is lame.  This computer connects to a router that randomly
disconnects from the internet, so I don't play nethack on a server. 
If I die a couple of times, I delete nethack and re-install it so I
don't get bone piles.

I started as a chaotic male elf wizard.

I started the game collecting daggers and trying on all uncursed
non-metallic armor.  I found a wand of speed and enchanted leather
armor before Minetown.  Leather armor weighs alot at this point of the
game, so I don't think I put it on yet.  I always walk around with a
pick-axe, which takes up alot of my carry weight.  A stack of daggers
isn't very light either.

Minetown had nothing useful, and the altar was co-aligned.  I was able
to donate to the priest once.  Most games I only can donate to the
priest once.  I'm not entirely sure how you are supposed to have alot
of money at this point.  Maybe digging the hell out of levels looking
for vaults?

Dungeon level 10 of the mines is probably the level that gave me the
most trouble.  I had 4 pets at dungeon level 9 of the mines.  I'm
horrible at getting pets to the bottom of the mines, so I usually
collect alot of them.  Most get separated from me well before I reach
the bottom of the mines, so I don't worry about any of them starving.

Even though I had a magic whistle, all 4 pets didn't want to descend
to level 10 at the same time.  So I went back and forth between L9 and
L10 until all 4 pets were in L10.  Well I thought all 4 pets were in
L10.  Two of them have already disappeared.  It turns out there is a
level teleport trap really close to the stairs.  Ran up a couple
squares and blew the magic whistle to make sure the other 2 don't get
lost.  I found a polymorph trap near the top of the screen.  Said
"wow, this is great!  I get to polymorph the hell out of my pets".

Started trying to polymorph my pets.  One of my pets died, but I
couldn't see what killed it.  Walked a couple squares and noticed a
Black dragon, some other 'D', and a couple other monsters which I
really can't kill at this point.  Ran like hell to the other side of
the level.  My last pet died along the way.  Went to L11.

I decided I might as well keep going to the bottom of mines.  My AC
isn't great, and force bolt is still my best spell.  Hopefully I can
collect more pets before I have to go back to L10, so they can
distract the horde of enemies in L10.  Getting the luckstone ended up
being easy.  Picked up an engravable gem next to the luckstone. 
Getting back to L10 ended up being easy.

I wasn't able to find anymore pets, and I really don't want to try and
walk past the black dragon since I still don't have telepathy. 
Without telepathy I'd probably get disintegrated before I could see
the black dragon with infravision.  Decided to dig a tunnel along the
entire bottom edge of the level.

I ran to where I wanted to start the tunnel.  I dug a couple of
squares before monsters started to catch up to me.  It takes a couple
turns to dig 1 square, and monsters really don't want to sit back and
watch you dig.  I ended up thinking up a really ghetto Elbereth
stragety.  I am at the dead end of the tunnel now.  I walked 2 squares
toward the entrance of the tunnel, wrote Elbereth in the dust 5 times,
and dropped a light object (i.e. a single gold piece).  I walked 1
square toward the dead end, engraved Elbereth on that square, and
dropped another small object. I walked 1 square toward the dead end,
and now I'm at the dead end.  Now I can dig part of the tunnel with
the pick-axe.  Baseically, writing Elbereth in the dust gave me enough
time to engrave Elbereth, and engraving Elbereth gave me enough time
to dig with my pick-axe.

I've dug some more squares of my tunnel, and a tengu teleports over to
me.  I can't melee a tengu at this point.  I am at the dead end of the
tunnel at this point.  I wrote Elbereth in the dust to get the tengu
away from me.  Walked one square away from the dead end, wrote
Elbereth 5 times in the dust, and dropped a small object.  Went back
to the dead end.  The tengu is still bouncing around, but it can't
reach me because I'm surrounded by 3 walls and an Elbereth square.
Since I dug the tunnel in a straight line, when the tengu flees it is
still lined up with me.  I force bolt the tengu to death.

I continued to dig the tunnel to the other side of the level.  A
couple of times along the way monsters got generated between me and
the closest Elbereth square, so I had to remake more Elbereth squares.
 At the end of my tunnel I saw a Dragon!  'D's can blast you from
across the screen even if you engrave Elbereth!  Fortunatly, I made
the end of the tunnel a bit jagged in case something like this
happened.  If the whole tunnel was in a straight line, the 'D'
probably would have blasted me from the tunnel entrance.  I went
around a corner of the tunnel and blocked it from the 'D' with
Elbereth.  I dug another tunnel going toward the top of the screen,
went around the 'D', and got to L9!

I got back to the main dungeon without a problem.  Went back up to L1
and found all the pets I lost in the game due to level teleport traps.
 Retamed 2 pets, and brought them to sokoban.  Sokoban was easy.  The
most exciting part of sokoban was that I got telepathy from a floating
eye corpse there.  Got a bag of holding from sokoban.

Went back to the main dungeon.  Went down a couple of levels and found
a store with speed boots. Those speed boots would have been great on
L10 of the mines!  Went down a couple more levels and found a
pyrolisk.  For some reason I didn't know pyrolisks have a ranged
attack.  Got blasted by the pyrolisk from across the screen.  Some of
my stuff got lost in the blast.  Killed the pyrolisk.

My force bolt spell is getting faint.  I tryed to get my force bolt
spellbook out of my bag of holding, but my bag is gone.  I think the
pyrolisk might have blasted my bag.  A couple turns later and I can't
use force bolt anymore.  I have no other attack spellbooks.  I put on
metal armor and readied my stack of daggers.  I went through all the
levels I've done so far (except anything past L9 in the mines), and
collected all the spellbooks.  I put all 5 books in a line (one on
each square) and zapped them with a wand of polymorph.  I read the new
books and rezapped the books.  At some point I got a spellbook of
Fireball, so now I can go back to using my spells.  I went back to my
normal armor too.

I was getting worried that I wouldn't find an altar outside of the
mines.  I really didn't want to deal with killing the minetown priest.
Fortunatly I found an altar at around L11 of the main dungeon.  I
converted the altar, and the previous god sent a divine being at me. 
Fortunatly, divine beings don't know how to open doors... because I
was able to shut it in a room.  I then sacrificed stuff until I got
crowned.  I got Magicbane, two worthless artifacts, and a bunch of
spellbooks I didn't need.  I have Fireball now, so I can kill all that
stuff in L10 of the mines now!  Fireball and Cone of cold are uber
because they are ranged spells that you can cast without being lined
up with the enemy. Since 'D's can only attack in a line, you can kill
them with Fireball/Cone of cold even if you couldn't survive their
ranged attack.

Went back to L1 and retamed the rest of the pets.  I brought 4 pets to
L9 of the mines.  I killed all the polymorphed enemies at L10, brought
the 4 pets to L10 (this time I might have dropped a cursed item on the
level teleport trap so they wouldn't go there), and started
polymorphing my pets at the polymorph trap.  One of the pets turned
into a mind flayer.  One of the pets turned into a succubus, so I
chatted with that until it got a severe headache.  I repolyed the
succubus.  At one point I got a dragon, but I repolyed it because I
really don't want more than one pet that can go feral from hunger.  I
ended up with a mind flayer, clay golem, air elemental, and the 4th
pet refused to turn into anything useful.  I repolyed the 4th pet into
something lame in case I had to kill it later.

I had my pets kill the divine being on the altar level.  It had a
shield of reflection.  The Air Elemental got killed shortly after from
some monster zapping it with a wand of foo.

I wasn't XL14 yet, so I went to the fort level. I forgot that a
soldier beyond the 2nd room of the fort usually has a death wand.  The
death ray DIAGONALLY bounced off multiple walls and killed my master
mind flayer.  The death ray started in the 2nd room of the fort (near
the doorway to the big open area), and ended in the 1st room of the
fort (near the magic portal).  I couldn't line a diagonal multi-wall
death shot like that if I tried.  I have one pet now, and I really
should make sure it doesn't die because I want a pet with me when I do
the quest.

I went through the dungeon having my clay golem kill all the unicorns.
 Then I zapped all the unicorn horns with a wand of polymorph.  I got
one magic marker, but it didn't have enough charges to write a
spellbook of polymorph.  One of the amulets I polymorphed ended up
being an amulet of change... now I'm female.

I went to the quest level, and quaffed a blessed potion of gain level
to get to XL14.  I found a magic marker during the quest.  Since I
still haven't ID'ed a light scroll, and I don't have the light spell
yet, I wrote a light scroll and used it on the stairs above the
nemesis level.  The problem with Fireball/Cone of cold is that you
can't target a dark area.  So if the nemesis escapes up the stairs, I
need the stairs above the nemesis level lit so I can still use
fireball.  The Nemesis died before he could escape up the stairs. 
Went back to the main dungeon.

The marker I got from the quest didn't have enough charges either. I
IDed a couple scrolls and found a charging scroll.  Blessed the
scroll, charged the marker, and wrote the book of polymorph. 
Polypiled the amulets I've collected so far and got an amulet of
reflection and an amulet of life saving.  I put on the amulet of life
saving.

I went back to the fort.  I killed the hoard of '@' in the doorway, so
I had a massive amount of equipment on 1 square.  I started polypiling
that square.  I pulled out a robe, a cloak of magic resistance, a
crystal plate mail, a shirt, and possibly a helm of brillance.  The
pile is down to a couple items now. I set aside the cloak and mail.  I
walked a couple of squares toward the fort, and totally forgot about
the black dragon on the level.  The dragon blasted me and I lost my
cloak and armor.  I put on the new cloak, crystal mail, and amulet of
reflection.  I should have put on the robe, but I forgot both my quest
artifact and my dagger give magic resistance.  I want a silver dragon
scale mail now because I want to wear the amulet of life saving
instead of the amulet of reflection.  Killed the black dragon.  I
accidently killed the first silver dragon over water, and the second
silver dragon didn't give scales.  Enchanted the black dragon scales
and wore that instead.  Finished the fort.

Made another run through the dungeon up to this point, collecting
stuff to be polypiled.  Polypiled scrolls to get enchant armor
scrolls.  Wrote some more enchant armor scrolls.  Polypiled amulets to
get life saving amulets.  Polypiled wands to get wands of
digging/teleportation/cancellation.  Got a helm of opposite alignment
from one of the polypiles.

I reached Medusa's level and noticed I still didn't have levitation
boots/rings.  I used cone of cold to reach Medusa, and fortunatly one
of the statues there had levitation boots.

Everything in the castle died easily.  I got 6 wishes total from the
castle wand.  First wish was for Silver dragon scale mail, since none
of the silver dragons wanted to drop scales. Second wish was for a
magic marker.  4 wishes were wasted on failed master key artifact
attempts.

I genocided all 'h' and all 'L'.  I then walked all the way back to my
altar stash, picking up all the potions along the way.  I invoked my
quest artifact to warp to Sokoban, read 2 cursed scrolls of genocide,
and reverse-genocided a bunch of nurses.  The nurses raised my max HP
by alot.

I went back to my altar stash and decided I wanted to blank some
potions so I could have alot of holy water.  I ran out of fountains (I
drank from alot of them to see if they were magic fountains, and the
rest I dried up from dipping stuff into them).  So I polymorphed into
a winged gargoyle, floated over a pool of water, and blanked the
potions.  I made a bunch of holy water potions, which I used to bless
my equipment.  The leftover water potions I tried to alchemy into gain
level potions, and botched twice before I realized you can't create a
stack of full healing potions by dipping a stack of water potions into
a potion of full healing.  I noticed I somehow got kicked down to
XL14. I don't know when I dropped XL, and I don't think botching
alchemy can drop XL.  I decided not to bother with raising XL anymore,
since I'm still not sure why people recommend Wizards try to gain XL
past 14.

Nothing exciting happened from this point to the vibrating square. 
Maybe something exciting should have happened, but Cone of Cold really
blasts the hell out of everything.  I picked up a charm monster
spellbook right before meeting Rodney, which is good because now I can
use the rest of my magic marker charges to write gold detection
scrolls.

Nothing exciting happened in Moloch's Sanctum.  After getting the
amulet, I drank a potion of cursed gain level to warp up a level. 
Went back to my altar stash.  This time I didn't botch the alchemy,
and made some full healing potions.  I picked up parts of the stash I
left behind for the final levels, and went to the Earth plane.  I
still had a wand of cold in my bag.  I don't know why I have a wand of
cold, so I polyed it.

Earth plane: Read confused scroll of gold detection to find the magic
portal.  I used my wands of digging to dig through the plane, and used
Charm Monster on whatever got near me.  I think I picked up a crystal
orb here.  Went to the portal, waited until I recharged to full MP,
and went in the portal

Air plane: Used crystal orb to find the magic portal.  Read confused
scroll of taming to tame all those air elementals that were coming at
me.  Used Charm Monster on whatever got near me.  Went to the portal,
waited until I recharged to full MP, and went in the portal

Fire plane: Used crystal orb.  Used Charm Monster on whatever got near
me. Took off my levitation boots to pick something off the floor. 
Forgot to put the boots back on and got stuck in lava.  Went into my
bag of holding to pull out my wand of cold.  Realized that I polyed my
wand of cold right before I got to the Earth Plane.  Didn't cone of
cold since that might kill pets.  My amulet of life saving crumbled,
which cleared the lava from the square I was on.  I put on another
amulet of life saving, then went to the water plane.

Water plane: Read confused scroll of gold detection. Walked a bit.
Read confused scroll of gold detection.  Walked a bit. Found the
portal. Ate food.  Waited until I recharged to full MP.  Lost the
portal.  Read confused scroll of gold detection.  Walked a bit. Read
confused scroll of gold detection. Found the portal.  Went in the
portal.

Astral plane:  The Death rider was in the middle area, so I decided to
go to the left area.  Death is the only '&' I don't like because
neither teleportation nor finger of death works on it.  Armed with 46
wand charges of teleportation, I zapped all the 'A' out of my path
with a teleportation wand.  '&' and '@' I hit with finger of death. 
Left altar was neutral.  Went back to the beginning of the level. 
Walked about 10 squares to the right.  Read a couple of confused
create monster scrolls to block the path behind me with acid blobs. 
Ran to the right altar blasting stuff with a teleportation wand or
finger of death.  Right altar was lawful.  I still had a bunch of
teleportation wand charges left, all my full healing potions, and 3
amulets of life saving.  Decided to put on my helm of opposite
alignment and offer the amulet.

